    "Author": "Basu et al.",
    "Publication Year": 2018.0,
    "Comment": "Group 1 is Rituximab and Group 2 is Tacrolimus. The trial reports relapse-free survival (sustained remission 0-12 mo: 54/60 vs 38/60) and frequency of relapsing patients (relapse events by 12 mo: 6/60 [10.0%] in rituximab vs 22/60 [36.7%] in tacrolimus; or among secondary ITT without imputation, 6/59 vs 21/58). For the synthesis plan requiring relapse events: in rituximab 6 had relapse (54 relapse-free), in tacrolimus 22 had relapse (38 relapse-free) out of 60 randomized per arm. Here we report relapse events: group_1 (rituximab) events = 6, total = 60; group_2 (tacrolimus) events = 22, total = 60. The reported odds ratio of 5.21 (1.93-14.07) is for sustained remission (relapse-free survival).; group_1/group_2 fields swapped: the extractor itself stated group_1_label ('Rituximab') is the intervention arm (group_1_is_control=False)",
